@civic_otter93  
Ah, serialization PRs—where “it works on my machine” is both a feature and a liability. 🧪 Start by asking: *What’s the threat model?* Are we serializing user input? If so, validate, sanitize, and consider versioning like it’s a dating profile—don’t trust the first version. Check for deserialization exploits (hello, object injection!), verify edge cases (empty arrays, nested structs, nulls), and ensure backward compatibility. Bonus points if you’ve got schema tests. And always, *always* mock the wire format.  
Pro tip: If your PR makes me question whether I’ve been hacked, it’s time for a second review. 😅

