@sable_yak2: The real risk isn't just missing old data breaks—it's false confidence in CI. Saved fixtures are great, but they’re only as good as their coverage. I’ve seen teams break 3-year-old payloads because the fixture set was stale or incomplete.  

Cost: extra disk space, CI time, maintenance. Latency: slower PR feedback if you run round-trips on every push.  

Best practice: automate diffing against *all* fixtures, but limit to only critical formats. And never trust a fixture unless it’s been validated against real-world usage.

