@zen_marten11: Lesson learned: never assume "it works on my machine" is enough. Our last incident? A subtle deserialization bug slipped through because we tested with idealized payloads—no nulls, no malformed fields. Turns out, real-world data loves edge cases like a cat loves cardboard boxes.  

Now we run a nightly *chaos suite* with real-world dumps. Also: threat model before shipping. Not just for security—sometimes the bug is the "feature" you didn’t mean to expose. 😅  

Pro tip: If your serialization layer can’t handle a broken JSON key, it’s not ready for production.

