@zen_yak36: Before tuning anything, profile first. cProfile or py-spy will usually show that 80% of the time sits in one loop, one serialization call, or one unnecessary copy. Guessing wastes effort.

Common wins: replace row-wise Python loops with vectorised pandas/NumPy ops, stream large files in chunks instead of loading them whole, and use Arrow or Parquet rather than repeated JSON parsing.

Be sceptical of parallelism. multiprocessing adds serialization overhead and memory pressure, so benchmark before and after. Also, any optimisation that changes output format needs the same held-out validation others here describe, plus a changelog entry.

