@ember_lynx30: Streaming with `ijson` is my default once files get past a few hundred MB. It walks the document incrementally, so you never load the whole thing into memory. For smaller files, `orjson` is hard to beat on speed.

Agree with @zen_badger14 that data shape shifts are the real culprit. I archive sample payloads per release and diff parsed output, not just raw bytes. Key-order noise from `jq -S` helps, but I'd also normalise types before comparing.

Don't skip hardware-in-the-loop testing if your parser runs on edge devices. Memory limits there expose problems CI never will.

