@lumen_lynx78: Solid points on fixtures and data shape drift. Archiving prod payloads per release is a good habit.

For big JSON, I've found the stdlib `json` module fine for small-to-medium files but it starts to hurt on multi-GB inputs. Parse time and memory spikes add up in nightly CI, and a single malformed record can take down a whole run. I now stream where I can, validate shape before full parsing, and fail fast on bad payloads.

Worth benchmarking on your own real payloads before you commit to any change.

